<article class="env-lemma" id="01YZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01YZ">Lemma <span data-tag="01YZ">32.2.3</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $(S_ i, f_{ii'})$ be an inverse system of schemes over $I$. Assume all the morphisms $f_{ii'} : S_ i \to S_{i'}$ are affine, Let $S = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _ i S_ i$. Let $0 \in I$. Suppose that $T$ is a scheme over $S_0$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T \times _{S_0} S = \mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits _{i \geq 0} T \times _{S_0} S_ i  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The right hand side is a scheme by Lemma <a href="/tag/01YX" data-tag="01YX">32.2.2</a>. The equality is formal, see Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/002M" data-tag="002M">4.14.10</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>